    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42472" root="يسر" body-key="Y">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">موسِرٌ</span></b>  [originally <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُيْسِرٌ</span>,] <i>Possessing competence,</i>
or <i>sufficiency;</i> or <i>rich,</i> or <i>wealthy,</i> or <i>opulent:</i>
(M, K:) pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَيَاسِيرُ</span>: (Sb, M, K:) [like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَفَالِيسُ</span>,
pl. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُفْلِسٌ</span>; and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَفَاطِيرُ</span>, pl. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُفْطِرٌ</span>; as though
the sing. were <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَيْسُورٌ</span>:] but by rule it should be
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُوسِرُونَ</span>, for the masc., and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُوسِرَاتٌ</span> for the fem.
(Abu-l-Hasan, M.)

